Feature: form-components-example
Target module: FormComponents (vUX-formComponents.js)

Added examples/form/ — a runnable demo exercising all six FormComponents builders
(select, radio, checkbox, datePicker, slideSwitch, file), following the existing
examples/modal/ convention. The demo was verified end-to-end in headless Chromium:
18 scripted interaction checks covering option search/selection, optgroups, multiple
select, refreshSelect(), radio/checkbox forwarding, the full date drill-down
(including 29-day February 2024 and weekday tooltips), datetime-local time entry,
switch toggling, slideSwitch.refresh() on injected markup, and file selection — all
passing with zero console errors.

Driving the example surfaced four more library defects, fixed here:
1. Checkbox widgets collapsed to zero height (static .vCheckboxWrapper height:auto beat
   the generated size; same line was already commented out for the radio wrapper).
2. Radio widgets were invisible (the circle-drawing ::before rule had no content
   property; the checkbox equivalent already had it).
3. Opening a date picker with a decade-series view (any span > 11 years, including the
   defaults) threw a ListScroller setup error — the picker configured a nonexistent
   property name (inactiveButtonsClassName vs inactiveButtonClassName) plus two other
   nonexistent properties, and its buttons lacked the vListBt classes the scroller's
   click handler requires. The error also aborted the open picker's z-index raise.
4. Configured style strings silently lost every CSS-cascade tie to the static
   stylesheet defaults (the link loads after the generated styles), e.g. a configured
   radio color rendered black and the checkbox check glyph never appeared. Generated
   selectors are now anchored to the wrapper base class so configured styles override
   defaults, per the documented contract.

Docs updated: example linked from doc/form-components.md and doc/README.md; the
style-override contract stated in the guide.

Affected projects: any consumer of vUX-formComponents.js / formComponents.css. The
specificity change means explicitly-configured style properties that previously lost
ties to static defaults now apply (e.g. myinvitees.com's configured slide-switch
wrapper border will now render as configured). Deployed library copies must be
re-synced to pick up the fixes.
